# gitleaks fingerprint ignores for Blotto Cup.
#
# ONE entry per finding, keyed by the finding's fingerprint —
# `<commit>:<path>:<rule>:<line>`. A fingerprint names an immutable point in
# history, so an entry here can never excuse anything but the exact finding it
# was written for. A new leak, in any file, of any shape, still fails the lane.
#
# Nothing is added here without the scrutiny `.gitleaks.toml` demands. That file
# records why the predecessor repository's allowlist was deliberately not
# carried, and the same bar applies: an entry states what the value is, why it
# is not a secret, and how that was established.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The seven below: `leaf_order` in the scoring known-vectors, commit 363fd042,
# 2026-08-27.
#
# WHAT THEY ARE. Not credentials. `backend/scoring/fixtures/vectors.json` is the
# Python-generated known-vector file every payout is checked against, and
# `leaf_order` is the results-tree leaf ordering for a pool — a list of PLAYER
# INDICES. A full pool is 64 players, so it is a 64-element array of small
# integers. That is published data by design: a player must be able to recompute
# what they were paid from it (CLAUDE.md, tradeoff #3).
#
# WHY THE RULE FIRES. `solana-keypair-json` matches a JSON array of exactly 64
# numbers, because that is the shape of a Solana secret key. A 64-player pool's
# leaf ordering has the identical shape. The rule cannot tell them apart, and it
# should not be loosened to try: it was written in the predecessor repository
# after a real committed keypair that the default ruleset missed entirely.
#
# WHY ONLY THIS COMMIT. At 363fd042 the fixtures were pretty-printed, one number
# per line; the rule's `\s*` spans newlines, so the array matched across 64 of
# them. The generator now emits `"leaf_order": "3,7,11,..."` as a compact STRING,
# so no array exists at HEAD and the working-tree scan is clean. These seven are
# a closed historical set that can never grow.
#
# HEADS UP. If the fixture generator is ever changed back to emitting
# `leaf_order` as an array, this rule will fire again on the new commits with
# new fingerprints, and the lane will go red. That is the gate working. Re-read
# this block before concluding it is the same false positive — check the file and
# the rule, do not just append fingerprints.
#
# Established 2026-09-13 by reading the flagged lines at that commit: the
# enclosing JSON keys are index / score_half / zones / rank / amount_lamports /
# leaf_order. No key material of any kind is present.

